{"slug": "tacos-with-black-beans-and-chard", "nyt_id": 12182, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/12182-tacos-with-black-beans-and-chard", "name": "Tacos With Black Beans and Chard", "author": "Martha Rose Shulman", "description": "If you are looking to feed a crowd, one way to meet the challenge is to pick up a supply of corn tortillas and make a big pot of beans and some other dishes that are at home in a taco. Buy some salsa, or make your own, and your house will be taco party central. You can make fillings in advance and arrange in bowls or on platters. Then all it takes is warming tortillas in a microwave, oven or steamer, and guests can assemble their own tacos. These beans are great in tacos, but can also be eaten on their own.", "servings": {"text": "6 to 8 servings. ", "min": 6, "max": 8, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 120, "raw": {"total": "2 hours"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 pound black beans, soaked for 4 to 6 hours or overnight in 2 quarts water", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "black beans", "preparation": "soaked for 4 to 6 hours or overnight in 2 quarts water", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 onion, chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "onion", "preparation": "chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "4 garlic cloves, minced", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "garlic cloves", "preparation": "minced", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "Salt to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 bunch cilantro, roughly chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "bunch", "item": "cilantro", "preparation": "roughly chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "½ pound Swiss chard, stemmed, washed and roughly chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "swiss chard", "preparation": "stemmed, washed and roughly chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "12 to 16 corn tortillas", "group": null, "quantity": 12.0, "quantity_max": 16.0, "unit": null, "item": "corn tortillas", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "Fresh or bottled salsa", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "fresh or bottled salsa", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "2 to 3 ounces queso fresco, crumbled", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": 3.0, "unit": "oz", "item": "queso fresco", "preparation": "crumbled", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Place the beans and their soaking water in a heavy soup pot or Dutch oven and bring to a boil. Skim away foam and add the onion and half the garlic. Reduce the heat, cover and simmer 1 hour. Add the remaining garlic, salt to taste and half the cilantro, cover and simmer for 45 minutes."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Add the Swiss chard, cover and simmer 10 minutes. The chard should be tender but still have some bright color. Stir in the remaining cilantro, taste and adjust salt."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Warm the tortillas. Top with a generous spoonful of beans with chard, a spoonful of crumbled queso fresco, and salsa if desired."}], "nutrition": null, "tags": {"cuisine": ["mexican"], "diet": ["gluten-free", "healthy", "high fiber", "low-fat", "low-sodium", "vegetarian"], "course": ["main course"], "meal": ["dinner", "lunch"], "occasion": [], "other": ["black bean", "low cholesterol", "tortilla"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2011/12/19/health/nutrition/19recipehealth/19recipehealth-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "Soft Tacos With Black Beans and Chard", "primary": true}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 233}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2011-12-19", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T23:53:31.059475+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "tacos-with-roasted-vegetables-and-chickpeas-in-chipotle-ranchera-salsa", "nyt_id": 12184, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/12184-tacos-with-roasted-vegetables-and-chickpeas-in-chipotle-ranchera-salsa", "name": "Tacos With Roasted Vegetables and Chickpeas in Chipotle Ranchera Salsa", "author": "Martha Rose Shulman", "description": "These winter vegetables sweeten with roasting and contrast beautifully with the chipotle-spiked cooked tomato salsa. It’s another easy do-ahead dish that can be reheated when the crowds are hungry.", "servings": {"text": "6 servings.", "min": 6, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 75, "raw": {"total": "1 hour 15 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 pound butternut squash, peeled and cut in ¾-inch dice", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "butternut squash", "preparation": "peeled and cut in ¾-inch dice", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "2 medium turnips (about 10 ounces), peeled and cut in ¾-inch dice", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "medium turnips (about 10 ounces)", "preparation": "peeled and cut in ¾-inch dice", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 medium fennel bulb, cored and cut in ¾-inch dice", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "medium fennel bulb", "preparation": "cored and cut in ¾-inch dice", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "2 tablespoons plus 1 teaspoon extra virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "plus 1 teaspoon extra virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "Salt and freshly ground pepper to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt and freshly ground pepper to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 red onion, cut in ¾-inch dice", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "red onion", "preparation": "cut in ¾-inch dice", "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 can chickpeas, drained and rinsed (optional)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "can", "item": "chickpeas", "preparation": "drained and rinsed", "optional": true}, {"position": 8, "raw": "12 corn tortillas", "group": null, "quantity": 12.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "corn tortillas", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "2 ounces queso cotija, queso fresco or feta", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "oz", "item": "queso cotija", "preparation": "queso fresco or feta", "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "1 small onion, cut in half, or .5 medium onion", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "small onion", "preparation": "cut in half, or .5 medium onion", "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "1 14-ounce can tomatoes, with juice", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "14-ounce can tomatoes", "preparation": "with juice", "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "1 or 2 serrano chilies or jalapeños (more to taste), seeded for a milder salsa, roughly chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "or 2 serrano chilies or jalapeños (more to taste)", "preparation": "seeded for a milder salsa, roughly chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "1 garlic clove, roughly chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "garlic clove", "preparation": "roughly chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 14, "raw": "1 chipotle chili in adobo, stemmed", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "chipotle chili in adobo", "preparation": "stemmed", "optional": false}, {"position": 15, "raw": "1 tablespoon canola oil", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "canola oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 16, "raw": "Salt to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 17, "raw": "Water as needed", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "water as needed", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Preheat oven to 400 degrees. Cover a large sheet pan with foil, and oil the foil. Place all of the vegetables except the onions in a large bowl, season with salt and pepper and toss with the olive oil until all of the vegetables are coated. Spread in an even layer on the prepared pan. Place in the top third of the oven and bake 20 minutes, stirring halfway through. Meanwhile, rinse the onion, drain on paper towels and toss with a teaspoon of olive oil."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Add the onions to the vegetables and toss together. Turn the heat down to 375, move the baking pan to the middle rack and continue to bake until the vegetables are lightly browned on the edges and tender all the way through when pierced with a knife, about 10 to 15 minutes. Transfer to a bowl and add the chickpeas if using."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Make the salsa while the vegetables are roasting. Preheat the broiler. Line a baking sheet with foil and place the onion on it. Broil 5 to 10 minutes, turning once, until charred. Remove from the heat and when cool enough to handle, cut in large dice and place in a blender with the tomatoes, serranos, garlic and chipotle. Purée until smooth."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Heat the canola oil in a heavy saucepan or skillet over medium-high heat until a drop of the puree sizzles immediately on contact. Add the purée, season to taste with salt and cook, stirring often, until the sauce darkens and thickens, leaving a canal when you run the cooking spoon across the bottom of the pan, about 15 minutes. If you want a thinner sauce, thin out with water as needed. Remove from heat. Taste and adjust salt."}, {"position": 5, "text": "Warm the tortillas. Stir some of the salsa (to taste) into the vegetables. Spoon onto the tortillas, sprinkle on the cheese and serve, with more salsa as desired."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 394.6, "protein_g": 12.5, "carbohydrates_g": 59.5, "fat_g": 14.2, "saturated_fat_g": 3.0, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 9.4, "sodium_mg": 973.3, "fiber_g": 13.5, "sugar_g": 11.8, "unsaturated_fat_g": 9.8, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["mexican"], "diet": ["gluten-free", "healthy", "high fiber", "vegetarian"], "course": ["main course"], "meal": ["dinner", "lunch"], "occasion": [], "other": ["broil", "butternut squash", "chickpea", "chipotles in adobo", "fall", "fennel", "roast", "saute", "tacos", "turnip"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2011/12/20/science/21recipehealth/21recipehealth-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 52}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2011-12-20", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T23:53:33.739502+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "tagliatelle-with-ham-and-fava-beans", "nyt_id": 10449, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/10449-tagliatelle-with-ham-and-fava-beans", "name": "Tagliatelle With Ham and Fava Beans", "author": "Moira Hodgson", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 10, "raw": {"total": "10 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 pound fresh tagliatelle", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "fresh tagliatelle", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 pound fava beans, peeled", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "fava beans", "preparation": "peeled", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 cup heavy cream", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "heavy cream", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "3 tablespoons unsalted butter", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "unsalted butter", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "3 to 4 slices cooked ham, cut in strips", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": 4.0, "unit": "slice", "item": "cooked ham", "preparation": "cut in strips", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "Coarse salt and freshly ground pepper to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "coarse salt and freshly ground pepper to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "¾ cup of grated Parmesan cheese", "group": null, "quantity": 0.75, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "of grated parmesan cheese", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Bring six quarts salted water to boil for the tagliatelle. Steam the fava beans until barely tender. Set aside."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Combine heavy cream, butter and ham in small saucepan and heat. Season to taste with salt and pepper. Add the fava beans and set aside."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Cook the tagliatelle until al dente. Drain and mix with the ham sauce and serve additional Parmesan cheese separately."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 857.1, "protein_g": 37.7, "carbohydrates_g": 86.1, "fat_g": 42.7, "saturated_fat_g": 23.8, "trans_fat_g": 0.7, "cholesterol_mg": 205.8, "sodium_mg": 814.8, "fiber_g": 9.1, "sugar_g": 12.5, "unsaturated_fat_g": 14.6, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["italian"], "diet": [], "course": ["main course"], "meal": ["dinner", "lunch"], "occasion": ["easter"], "other": ["boil", "easy", "fava bean", "ham", "pastas", "quick", "steam"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 9}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1991-03-31", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T22:23:51.509602+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "taleggio-and-mushroom-tart", "nyt_id": 10591, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/10591-taleggio-and-mushroom-tart", "name": "Taleggio And Mushroom Tart", "author": "Florence Fabricant", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "6 servings", "min": 6, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 60, "raw": {"total": "1 hour"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 ¼ cups flour, plus more for rolling", "group": null, "quantity": 1.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "flour", "preparation": "plus more for rolling", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "½ teaspoon salt", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "6 tablespoons cold butter, preferably high-fat", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "cold butter", "preparation": "preferably high-fat", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 large egg yolk, beaten with 2 tablespoons ice water", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "large egg yolk", "preparation": "beaten with 2 tablespoons ice water", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 tablespoon extra virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "extra virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 teaspoon cumin seeds", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "cumin seeds", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "8 ounces shiitake mushrooms, sliced and stems discarded", "group": null, "quantity": 8.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "oz", "item": "shiitake mushrooms", "preparation": "sliced and stems discarded", "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "1 tablespoon finely sliced shallots", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "finely sliced shallots", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "Salt and ground white pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt and ground white pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "2 tablespoons creme fraiche", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "creme fraiche", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "6 ounces taleggio, rind removed, sliced thin", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "oz", "item": "taleggio", "preparation": "rind removed, sliced thin", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Heat oven to 400 degrees. Combine flour and salt in food processor. Pulse to combine. Dice butter, and add. Pulse until pebbly. Open lid, and sprinkle with egg yolk mixture. Pulse 10 or 12 times. If dough does not come together, sprinkle on a little more ice water and pulse again. Do not overwork."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Gather dough in a ball, flatten and roll out on floured board. Fit into an 8-or 9-inch tart pan. Prick bottom, line with parchment paper or foil, cover with pastry weights or dry beans and bake 10 minutes. Remove paper and weights. Bake about 10 minutes more, until pastry starts to color. Remove from oven. Reduce heat to 375 degrees."}, {"position": 3, "text": "While pastry bakes, heat oil in a 10-inch skillet. Add half the cumin seeds. When they pop, add mushrooms and shallots, and saute, stirring, until mushrooms start to brown. Season with salt and pepper."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Spread pastry with creme fraiche. Cover with mushrooms, and top with cheese slices. Scatter with remaining cumin. Bake in oven about 20 minutes, until cheese melts. Serve."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 338.8, "protein_g": 10.1, "carbohydrates_g": 24.1, "fat_g": 22.9, "saturated_fat_g": 12.6, "trans_fat_g"